course: dictionary
lesson: 1474
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One small word can have many meanings. Catch is a good example. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer means. «She had to catch the ball before it rolled into the pond.» Here catch means to take and hold something that is moving.
explain: «We ran to catch the bus before it left.» Now catch means to get on in time. The clue is the bus. A bus cannot be held in your hands, so the meaning must be different. Always ask: does this meaning fit the sentence?
explain: Catch also has phrases. «Mum said, "Wrap up warm, or you will catch a cold."» Catch a cold means to get a cold from someone or from the cold weather. When a phrase is new, read the whole phrase and the sentence around it, then try your meaning.
explain: Catch is a verb, so it changes: catches, caught, catching. It is also a noun: a catch. «The fishing boat came back with a big catch.» Here catch means the fish that were caught. When you see a new form of a word, check the sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: The same word can have several meanings, so always check the sentence before you decide.
fact: «Caught» is the past form of catch, as in «I caught him eating sweets».
fact: «Catch fire» means to start burning, as in «When the paper touched the flame, it caught fire».
fact: A catch can also mean a hidden problem, as in «What's the catch?».
exercise: «Sam had to catch the ball before it rolled out of the park.» What does catch mean here? | To make a loud ringing sound | To find a hidden hole in the grass | *To take and hold something that is moving
exercise: «We ran to catch the bus before it left the stop.» What does catch mean here? | To say something rude to the driver | *To get on in time | To look at something very closely
exercise: «Mum said, "Wrap up warm, or you will catch a cold."» What does catch a cold mean? | To see a shadow move | *To get a cold from someone or the weather | To hold a pencil tightly
test: «I caught him eating sweets before dinner.» What does caught mean here? | To hold something tightly | *To see or find someone doing something | To sing very loudly
test: «The fishing boat came back with a big catch.» What does catch mean here? | A game where you throw a ball | *The fish that were caught | A loud noise from the sea
exam: «When the paper touched the flame, it caught fire straight away.» What does caught fire mean? | *Started to burn | Fell off the table | Turned cold and wet
